# Review: Feeds

The spec states that the code does not implement this design yet. The code agrees: the feed layer has
no branches. The code has the base that the spec describes in "What exists":

- A `Feed` is an append log of ECHO objects.
- `Obj.update` appends the full object again by id.
- `FeedProtocol.Block` holds the fields that the spec names, and the `position` for each space and
  namespace.
- Soft fork (`Feed.PARENT_KEY`, `Feed.history`) gives a lineage for each item in one feed.

All the branch requirements are missing: removal, an index for each branch, heads, partial sync and
retention for each branch. Indexing, retention and sync apply only to a full feed.

The trajectory design (#13782) is not on `main`. The `Thread` 0.3.0 comment feeds (#14206) are also not
on `main`. Thus `Trajectory.Event` and `threadOpen` have no code in this checkout.

Of 20 items: 2 done, 0 untested, 5 partial, 1 diverged, 12 missing. These three findings are the most
important:

- **Rewind is a separate mechanism.** [F-1.5] tells that a rewind is a branch and a removal. The code
  does a rewind with `Feed.rewindFrom` and the `PARENT_KEY` lineage of each item. `Feed.history`
  resolves this lineage when it reads.
- **All options apply to a full feed.** `Feed.IndexingOptions`, `Feed.RetentionOptions`, `Feed.sync`
  and `Scope.feed` take a feed and no smaller unit. Thus [F-2.1], [F-2.3] and [F-4.4] have no hook for
  new code.
- **The code will remove local order.** `Block.insertionId` is the only local order. It has the comment
  `TODO(dmaretskyi): Remove. Use cursors.`. The local cursor API of #13782 is not on `main`.

