## Verdicts

```mdl
verdict F-1.1: A Feed is an append log of ECHO objects.
  status: done
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.ts#Feed, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.ts#append]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo-client-e2e/src/feed.test.ts]
```

```mdl
verdict F-1.2: Soft fork gives a lineage for each item in one feed. There are no branch ids or fork points.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.ts#PARENT_KEY, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.ts#history]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.test.ts]
  note: |
    The lineage needs no extra ECHO objects, as the requirement tells. `Feed.history` resolves one
    head back through its ancestors. A branch has no id, no parent branch and no stored fork point.
    The `Feed` object holds no map of branches.
```

```mdl
verdict F-1.3: Obj.update appends the full object again by id. The index keeps the latest block.
  status: done
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Obj.ts#update]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo-client-e2e/src/feed.test.ts]
```

```mdl
verdict F-1.4: You cannot remove a branch. Feed.remove puts a tombstone on one item.
  status: missing
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.ts#remove]
  note: We searched `Feed.ts`, the feed store and the indexer for a removed or hidden branch state. We found no such state.
```

```mdl
verdict F-1.5: Rewind is a separate mechanism, not a branch plus removal.
  status: diverged
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.ts#Feed, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.ts#history]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.test.ts]
  note: |
    `Feed.rewindFrom` on the Feed object holds a pending rewind. When `Feed.history` reads, it follows
    `PARENT_KEY` and removes the abandoned items. No code creates a branch or sets the old branch to
    removed.
```

```mdl
verdict F-2.1: Indexing is on or off for a full feed. A query cannot have a scope of branches.
  status: missing
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.ts#IndexingOptions, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Scope.ts#feed]
  note: |
    `Feed.IndexingOptions` has no subset mode. `Scope.feed` takes only a feed URI. The index has no
    branch column, thus a branch filter cannot run before `limit`.
```

```mdl
verdict F-2.2: The feed store has a head for each namespace, not for each branch.
  status: missing
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/feed/src/feed-store.ts#FeedStore]
  note: |
    The feed store gives an answer for a caught-up cursor, and it does not read blocks for this
    answer. It moves a head for each namespace (feed-store tests "answers a caught-up cursor…" and
    "moves the head of the namespace…"). No call gives the branches whose heads changed since a cursor.
```

```mdl
verdict F-2.3: Sync is for a full feed. A client cannot sync one branch.
  status: missing
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.ts#sync]
  note: '`Feed.sync` pulls the full feed. Blocks have no branch id that EDGE can use to select them.'
```

```mdl
verdict F-2.4: The EDGE position exists. The only local order is insertionId, and no API shows it.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/protocols/src/FeedProtocol.ts#Block]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/feed/src/feed-store.test.ts]
  note: |
    The position authority sets `position`, and the position converges. The local order is
    `insertionId`, and a comment marks it for removal. `Filter.feedCursor({ order: 'local' })` and
    `Feed.getLocalCursor` from #13782 are not on main.
```

```mdl
verdict F-3.1: AI chat, comments and messaging do not use one model.
  status: missing
  note: '`Chat`, `Thread` and `Channel` are separate ECHO types. Each type has its own feed and shape.'
```

```mdl
verdict F-4.1: No read has a scope of one branch. Thus privacy by construction is not possible at this time.
  status: missing
  note: There are no branches for the scope of a default read. A feed read gives all items.
```

```mdl
verdict F-4.2: Each block names its writer. We did not find a fixed turn view or a detection of late items.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/protocols/src/FeedProtocol.ts#Block, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.ts#history]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/feed/src/feed-store.test.ts]
  note: |
    Each block names its `actorId` and `sequence`. The soft-fork lineage is on each item, thus a fork
    does not misattribute a writer that did not see the fork. For concurrent `Obj.update` calls, the
    last flush wins. No code fixes the view of a turn when it starts. No code marks a late item
    (`PromptState.stale` is in #13782).
```

```mdl
verdict F-4.3: There is no branch to create.
  status: missing
  note: A soft fork costs one `PARENT_KEY` on an item that exists. But there is no branch record to count.
```

```mdl
verdict F-4.4: Retention applies only to a full feed.
  status: missing
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.ts#RetentionOptions]
  note: '`Feed.RetentionOptions` (`maxLength`, `maxAge`) applies to a full feed. There is no policy for each branch.'
```

```mdl
verdict F-4.5: Permissions apply to a full feed. A branch cannot have a smaller audience.
  status: missing
  note: We searched the Feed module and the feed store for an audience for each branch. We found none.
```

```mdl
verdict Block: FeedProtocol.Block has all the fields that the spec names.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/protocols/src/FeedProtocol.ts#Block]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/feed/src/feed-store.test.ts, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/protocols/src/FeedProtocol.test.ts]
  note: |
    The block has `actorId`, `sequence`, `prevActorId`, `prevSequence`, `timestamp`, `data`
    (ciphertext when sealed), `position` (for each space and namespace, with tests) and `insertionId`.
    #13782 adds a local order API for `insertionId`, and this API is not on main.
```

